Z||000004||fiero56||10-06-2000||08:48 PM||||A 3.2 is a 3.1 bored over.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jay||10-06-2000||08:52 PM||||3.2 seems fast but really is a waste of money, in my opinion.  At the track a guy in our club could only manage low 16's in a bored over 3.2  It feels real quick but to spend all that money on the re-build I think it would be wiser to go with the supercharged 3.8  If you got some money then you could even go with a Northstar V8.  Now that's an engine swap!!!!  Good Luck!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay||10-06-2000||09:28 PM||||Didn't mean to hurt anyone with that comment about a waste of money doing a 3.2  I guess what I ment to say is that's a good start, but I don't think you'll be happy with just a 3.2 But then again it depends on what you want to use it for.  Did anyone say NOS?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||10-06-2000||09:55 PM||||Jay, the Bonneville engine is not the cake walk you make it out to be.  It is a very hard swap.  The wiring is a mess.  The Northstar is in a different league.  The 3.2 is very easy and you can get nice Hp from it, same with the 3.4.  The 3.2 and 3.4 are considered bolt in because they use a lot of Fiero stuff.  The 3800 is a whole new engine, and you better hope you know how to fix it because I doubt a local mechanic would ever want to touch it...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||3
